hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"477","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, and Abu al-Mughirah, both saying: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you calls his brother and he says to him: At your service, let him not say: Before you, but let him say: May Allah answer you with what you love."
